# Arch/AUR packages for Linux (Omarchy), installed with `yay -S --needed`.
# The Linux counterpart of the Brewfile. One package per line; `#` starts a comment.
#
# Already provided by Omarchy, so not listed: git, gnupg, jq, imagemagick,
# postgresql (psql), starship, tmux, herdr, docker, 1password, chromium,
# ripgrep (replaces ack), fzf, zoxide, eza, bat.
#
# Runtimes (node, pnpm, go, bun, uv, python) come from mise, see linux/mise.toml.
#
# macOS-only casks with no Linux build: claude (desktop), raycast (use the
# Omarchy menu), readdle-spark, mas apps.
#
# Apps removed from the Brewfile in #65 (Ghostty, cmux, iTerm2, Supacode,
# TablePlus) are not wanted on any OS, so they are not listed here either.

# shell
zsh
zsh-autosuggestions
zsh-completions
zsh-history-substring-search
zsh-syntax-highlighting
zsh-autocomplete-git # AUR
zsh-you-should-use # AUR

# cli
act # GitHub Actions runner
git-delta # syntax-highlighting pager for git and diff output
git-lfs
grc # colorize logfiles and command output
just # Task runner
rtk # AUR: CLI proxy to minimize LLM token consumption
valkey # Redis-compatible in-memory database (Arch replaced redis with valkey)
wget

# apps
cursor-bin # AUR
discord
firefox
google-chrome # AUR
insomnia-bin # AUR
spotify # AUR
surfshark-client # AUR
ttf-firacode-nerd
ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd
zed
zoom # AUR
